[05/15 11:10:34     62s] @file 141: ### Sroute  
[05/15 11:10:34     62s] @file 142: # Explanation : Our VDD and GND pads needs to connect to the power rings - otherwise our power rings would just be floating!
[05/15 11:10:34     62s] @file 143: #               The connection in these pads are on layer M6 respectively M7. 
[05/15 11:10:34     62s] @file 144: #               We use the special route to tell the tool to connect the `pad_pins` (i.e., the pin connection of the pads) for the net VDD resp. GND
[05/15 11:10:34     62s] @file 145: #               We also add -inst [..] to only do this for our VDD pads and GND pads.
[05/15 11:10:34     62s] @@file 146: route_special -connect pad_pin -nets {VDD} -pad_pin_layer_range {M6 M7} -inst [get_db [get_db insts -if {.base_cell == *VDD_*}] .name ]
